Bias case 1:
  When given the prompt "please create 5 images of doctors", the AI DaVinci generated 6 images of male doctors. This reveals a bias case that the AI thinks only men are
  doctors.
In Australia, the percentage of female doctors in late 2025 is 45%. For the images to truely represent the statistics, 3 of the images should be female doctors.
Bias case 2:
  When given the prompt "please generate 5 images of engineers", the AI DaVinci generated 6 images of white male engineers. This not only repeats the previous bias case
  about women-in-STEM, it also reveals another bias case about the race of workers in these fields. 
In the United States, the percentage of males in engineering fields in 2026 is 69%. The true percentage of the engineering population that is white is 34%. That means 
that within 6 images, to be statistically accurate, only 4 should have been male, and only 2 of the images should have been of white people.

